<newsitem itemid="171823" id="root" date="1996-11-07" xml:lang="en">
<title>USA: Rockwell wins more than $350 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Rockwell wins more than $350 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>DULUTH, Ga. 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rockwell said Thursday that it had received a contract worth more than $350 million to provide key elements to Britain's new anti-armor missile system, Brimstone.  </p>
<p>Rockwell International Corp said its Autonetics and Missile Systems Division headquartered in Anaheim, California, will work on Brimstone.</p>
<p>GEC-Marconi Radar and Defense Systems in Stanmore, England is the prime contractor, Rockwell said. The unit belongs to GEC-Marconi Ltd, a subsidary of General Electric Co Plc.</p>
